@startuml environments-separation
title Environment isolation: one shared module, one root + state per environment
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

package "Repository — configuration only (evaluated at plan time; provisions nothing)" {
  component "modules/  (child module)\n---\nnetwork.tf  security.tf\niam.tf  ecr.tf  cluster.tf\ndata.tf  alb.tf  registry.tf\nservices.tf\n---\nall resource names derive from\n""name_prefix = agentd-${var.environment}""" as STACK

  package "environments/dev  (root module)" {
    component "main.tf\nmodule \"stack\" {\n  source      = \"../../modules\"\n  environment = \"dev\"\n}" as DEVMAIN
    database "terraform.tfstate\nresource records for the\nagentd-dev objects ONLY\n(address → AWS id mappings)" as DEVSTATE
  }
  package "environments/staging  (root module)" {
    component "main.tf\nmodule \"stack\" {\n  environment = \"staging\"\n}" as STGMAIN
    database "terraform.tfstate\nnot created yet —\nwritten by the first apply" as STGSTATE
  }
  package "environments/prod  (root module)" {
    component "main.tf\nmodule \"stack\" {\n  environment = \"prod\"\n}\nimage_tag_mutability = IMMUTABLE\necr_force_delete     = false" as PRODMAIN
    database "terraform.tfstate\nnot created yet" as PRODSTATE
  }
}

cloud "ONE AWS account" {
  frame "agentd-dev resources  (provisioned)" as AWSDEV {
    component "VPC 10.0.0.0/16 (own)\nALB agentd-dev\nECS cluster agentd-dev\nEFS, secret agentd/dev/app\nservices agentd-dev-*" as DEVRES
  }
  frame "agentd-staging resources  (none yet)" as AWSSTG {
    component "created by staging's first apply:\nseparate VPC, ALB agentd-staging, ..." as STGRES #line.dashed
  }
  frame "agentd-prod resources  (none yet)" as AWSPROD {
    component "created by prod's first apply:\nseparate VPC, ALB agentd-prod, ..." as PRODRES #line.dashed
  }
}

DEVMAIN  ..> STACK : module source\n(code reference only)
STGMAIN  ..> STACK : module source
PRODMAIN ..> STACK : module source

DEVMAIN  --> AWSDEV  : apply in this directory\noperates ONLY on these
STGMAIN  --> AWSSTG  : apply here creates/updates\nONLY these
PRODMAIN --> AWSPROD : apply here creates/updates\nONLY these

DEVSTATE <--> AWSDEV : state records map 1:1\nto these AWS objects

note bottom of STACK
  modules/ is a child module: parameterized resource
  declarations. Each environments/ directory is a
  root module that instantiates it (module "stack")
  with different input variables and maintains its
  own state file.
end note

note bottom of AWSDEV
  Isolation mechanisms, independent of each other:
  1. STATE SCOPE — plan/apply diffs THIS root's config
     against THIS root's state file. Other environments'
     resources are absent from both inputs, so no
     operation can reference them.
  2. NAMESPACING — resource names carry the agentd-<env>
     prefix and each environment provisions its own VPC,
     so identically-defined objects coexist in one
     account without name or network collisions.
end note
@enduml

@startuml apply-flow
title Execution: ""terraform apply"" in environments/dev
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

actor Operator
participant "terraform\n(cwd: environments/dev)" as TF
database "environments/dev/\nterraform.tfstate" as STATE
participant "AWS API" as AWS

Operator -> TF : terraform apply
TF -> TF : load config of the current root module\n→ module "stack" with environment = "dev"\n→ desired resource set, names agentd-dev-*
TF -> STATE : read this root's state file\n→ recorded resource set + AWS ids
TF -> TF : compute diff (desired vs recorded)\nmoved blocks rewrite addresses before the diff
note right of TF
  staging/prod are absent from BOTH diff inputs:
  not in this root's variables, not in this
  root's state. No API call can target them.
end note
TF -> AWS : Create/Update calls for the diff only,\nall objects named agentd-dev-*
AWS --> TF : resource ids
TF -> STATE : write updated records\n(still exclusively agentd-dev objects)

== First apply in environments/staging ==
Operator -> TF : terraform apply (cwd: environments/staging)
TF -> TF : desired set: agentd-staging-* (same module,\ndifferent variable value)
TF -> STATE : staging's state file: empty → recorded set = ∅
TF -> AWS : Create calls for the full resource set:\nnew VPC, ALB agentd-staging, cluster, EFS, ...
note right of TF
  dev unaffected: disjoint state file,
  disjoint names, disjoint VPC.
end note
@enduml
